---
/**
 * Field note: "Out of your box. Into mine."
 * → /field-notes/think-out-of-the-box-trap/
 *
 * Its own look, and none of the other four bare notes: a shipping crate.
 * Kraft board, corrugation stripes, stencil caps, rubber-stamp marks. The
 * note is about a box, so the page is one.
 *
 * The meme is two stamped crate panels, drawn here in CSS and type rather
 * than borrowed. The nine dots drawing is original SVG and shows the real
 * four-line solution, which is the whole reason the phrase existed.
 *
 * Shortest note on the site by design. It makes one point.
 *
 * Inter is already loaded site-wide (ThemeHead.astro); only Bebas Neue is
 * imported here.
 */
---

<div class="box">
  <div class="box-inner">
    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <section class="box-hero">
      <p class="box-kicker">Field note &middot; critical thinking</p>
      <h1>Out of your box.<br /><span class="box-hi">Into mine.</span></h1>
      <p class="box-dek">
        &ldquo;Think outside the box&rdquo; started as a good instruction. In
        most meetings it now means something else.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ THE MEME ============ -->
    <section class="box-meme" aria-label="Two panels: what they say, and what they mean">
      <div class="box-panel">
        <p class="box-panel-l">What they say</p>
        <p class="box-panel-q">&ldquo;We need to think outside the box.&rdquo;</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box-panel box-panel--alt">
        <p class="box-panel-l">What they mean</p>
        <p class="box-panel-q">&ldquo;My opinion is better than your opinion.&rdquo;</p>
        <p class="box-stamp" aria-hidden="true">Approved</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <p class="box-credit">
      Dileep Rao puts it sharper:
      <a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/dileeprao/">&ldquo;Get out of your box and get into my box.&rdquo;</a>
    </p>

    <!-- ============ 01 ============ -->
    <section class="box-card">
      <p class="box-num">01 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; The original</p>
      <h2>The phrase started out as a puzzle instruction.</h2>
      <p>
        It comes from the nine dots puzzle, used as a teaching metaphor since
        at least 1954. Nine dots in a three by three grid, four straight lines,
        connect all of them. Most people fail on the first attempt because they
        keep the lines inside the square the dots suggest. Nothing in the
        instructions puts them there.
      </p>

      <figure class="box-fig">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="box-dots">
          <title id="box-dots"
            >The nine dots puzzle. Nine dots sit in a three by three grid
            inside a faint square. Four straight lines connect all nine, and
            two of them run well past the edge of the square.</title
          >
          <rect x="88" y="28" width="144" height="144" class="d-box" />
          <g class="d-line">
            <path d="M110 50 L262 50" />
            <path d="M262 50 L108 204" />
            <path d="M108 204 L110 50" />
            <path d="M110 50 L212 152" />
          </g>
          <g class="d-dot">
            <circle cx="110" cy="50" r="7" /><circle cx="160" cy="50" r="7" /><circle cx="210" cy="50" r="7" />
            <circle cx="110" cy="100" r="7" /><circle cx="160" cy="100" r="7" /><circle cx="210" cy="100" r="7" />
            <circle cx="110" cy="150" r="7" /><circle cx="160" cy="150" r="7" /><circle cx="210" cy="150" r="7" />
          </g>
          <text x="160" y="226" text-anchor="middle" class="d-cap">the square nobody asked for</text>
        </svg>
        <figcaption>
          Norman Vincent Peale ran this in the Chicago Tribune in 1969: step
          outside the box your problem has created within you. The printed
          phrase followed in 1971.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="box-note">
        Consultants carried the puzzle into boardrooms through the 1970s and
        1980s. The story that it started inside Walt Disney is repeated
        everywhere and sourced nowhere. Wikipedia files it among the
        unconfirmed accounts, with no date and no document behind it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 02 ============ -->
    <section class="box-card">
      <p class="box-num">02 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; The trap</p>
      <h2>What the business version is actually asking for.</h2>
      <p>
        The original asks for the assumption nobody assigned. The business
        version tends to skip that step and arrive with the destination already
        picked. The phrase still wears the costume of the older meaning, which
        is why a request for agreement gets through as an invitation to think.
      </p>
      <p>
        The difference shows up in the wording. An invitation that means it
        will name the constraint it wants suspended. Without that, the phrase
        is doing no work that a plain statement of the preferred answer would
        not do better.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ 03: the test ============ -->
    <section class="box-card">
      <p class="box-num">03 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; The test</p>
      <h2>One question tells you which one you got.</h2>
      <p class="box-ask">&ldquo;Which assumption should I drop?&rdquo;</p>
      <p>
        A real invitation answers in a sentence. Assume we have no budget. Assume the
        biggest account walks in March. The other kind repeats the conclusion in
        different words, usually louder, and the meeting moves on without anyone
        naming what was supposed to change.
      </p>
      <table class="box-tbl">
        <caption>What each version of the request looks like in a meeting.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Opening a box</th><th scope="col">Defending one</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Names a constraint to suspend</td><td>Names an outcome to reach</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Survives a worse answer than expected</td><td>Only accepts one answer</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Asks what you assumed</td><td>Tells you what you missed</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ CLOSER ============ -->
    <section class="box-close">
      <p class="box-num">The rule</p>
      <p class="box-shout">The useful version of the phrase names a constraint.</p>
      <p>Ask for it by name, and you find out quickly which meeting you are in.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ TITLE BLOCK ============ -->
    <footer class="box-foot">
      <dl class="box-block">
        <div><dt>Note</dt><dd>The outside-the-box trap</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Field</dt><dd>Critical thinking</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Credit</dt><dd>Dileep Rao</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Ask</dt><dd>Which assumption?</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="box-foot-h">Go deeper</p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/dileeprao/">Dileep Rao at Forbes</a>.
        Clinical professor of entrepreneurship at Florida International
        University, and the source of the line this note is built on.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thinking_outside_the_box">Thinking outside the box</a>
        on Wikipedia. The attestation trail, the nine dots, and the unsourced
        Disney claim.
      </p>
      <p class="box-back">
        <a href="/field-notes/">← All field notes</a>
        <a href="/">aleberriz.com</a>
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bebas+Neue&display=swap');

  /* Shipping crate. Scoped, so none of this reaches another note. */
  .box {
    --kraft: #b78e5e;
    --board: #c9a476;
    --flap: #a87f51;
    --ink: #2a1c0d;
    --body: #40301c;
    --dim: #6f5636;
    --stamp: #a32319;
    --mark: #1b4a7a;

    min-height: 100vh;
    color: var(--body);
    font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    background-color: var(--kraft);
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      rgba(42, 28, 13, 0.07) 0 1px,
      transparent 1px 9px
    );
  }

  .box-inner {
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.15rem 3.5rem;
  }

  .box p { margin: 0 0 0.9rem; }
  .box a { color: var(--stamp); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .box a:hover { color: var(--mark); }

  .box-kicker,
  .box-num,
  .box-panel-l,
  .box-foot-h,
  .box-back,
  .box-block dt {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dim);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  /* ---------- hero ---------- */
  .box-hero { padding: 3.25rem 0 2rem; }
  .box-hero h1 {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 1rem;
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 15vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .box-hi { color: var(--stamp); }
  .box-dek {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: var(--body);
    max-width: 32ch;
  }

  /* ---------- the meme ---------- */
  .box-meme {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .box-panel {
    position: relative;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.1rem 1.3rem;
    background: var(--board);
    border: 3px solid var(--ink);
    box-shadow: 5px 5px 0 rgba(42, 28, 13, 0.32);
  }
  .box-panel--alt { background: var(--flap); padding-bottom: 2.9rem; }
  .box-panel-l {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    opacity: 0.72;
  }
  .box-panel-q {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 7vw, 2.15rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .box-panel--alt .box-panel-q { color: #1a1105; }
  .box-stamp {
    position: absolute;
    right: 0.5rem;
    bottom: 0.35rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--stamp);
    border: 2px solid var(--stamp);
    opacity: 0.75;
    transform: rotate(-7deg);
  }
  .box-credit {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--body);
  }

  /* ---------- sections ---------- */
  .box-card,
  .box-close {
    padding: 2.1rem 0;
    border-top: 2px dashed rgba(42, 28, 13, 0.3);
  }
  .box-card h2,
  .box-close h2 {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.9rem;
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 8vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: 0.015em;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .box-note {
    margin-top: 1.1rem;
    padding-left: 0.95rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--stamp);
    font-size: 0.96rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .box-ask {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 7vw, 2rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--mark);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* ---------- drawing ---------- */
  .box-fig { margin: 1.6rem 0 0; }
  .box-fig svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--board);
    border: 3px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .box-fig figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--dim);
  }
  .d-box {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--ink);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-dasharray: 6 6;
    opacity: 0.45;
  }
  .d-line path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--stamp);
    stroke-width: 3.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }
  .d-dot circle { fill: var(--ink); }
  .d-cap {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    fill: var(--dim);
  }

  /* ---------- table ---------- */
  .box-tbl {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 1.3rem 0 0;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }
  .box-tbl caption {
    caption-side: bottom;
    padding-top: 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--dim);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .box-tbl th,
  .box-tbl td {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
    border: 2px solid rgba(42, 28, 13, 0.3);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .box-tbl thead th {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: rgba(42, 28, 13, 0.08);
  }

  /* ---------- closer ---------- */
  .box-shout {
    font-family: 'Bebas Neue', Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 10vw, 3.1rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: 0.015em;
    color: var(--stamp);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* ---------- title block ---------- */
  .box-foot {
    padding: 2rem 0 0;
    border-top: 2px dashed rgba(42, 28, 13, 0.3);
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }
  .box-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 2px;
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
    background: rgba(42, 28, 13, 0.3);
    border: 2px solid rgba(42, 28, 13, 0.3);
  }
  .box-block > div { padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; background: var(--board); }
  .box-block dt { margin-bottom: 0.1rem; }
  .box-block dd { margin: 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .box-foot-h { margin-bottom: 0.55rem; color: var(--stamp); }
  .box-back { display: flex; gap: 1.4rem; padding-top: 0.9rem; }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .box-meme { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .box-block { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }

  /* ---------- present mode ---------- */
  :global(html.present) .box { font-size: 1.2rem; }
</style>
